extraction_notes: "WB19 Australia printed 70-72 (cache p071-p073, cache page = printed folio + 1), read in column order off the text layer. Heading Outbacker Runabout O.C.C. and the lore on printed 70; Special O.C.C. Skills of the Runabout on printed 70-71; the stat block headed Outbacker Runabout O.C.C., also known as a Drifter and sometimes the Australian Cowboy, Bush Cowboy or Cowpoke, on printed 71; it ends on printed 72 before the Raider. || GROUP: listed as Runabout O.C.C. under Outback O.C.C.s on printed 56; occ_group optional. || S.D.C.: the entry prints no Base S.D.C. line; its O.C.C. Bonuses print +4D6+6 S.D.C. That is stored as sdc_base 4d6+6, a reading: the class figure stands as the base, as the neighbouring Outback classes print theirs, and no men_of_arms line is needed. || XP: the Bushranger, Runabout, Infantry Grunt & City Police ladder on the Experience Tables, printed 224, read off a render. || BONUSES: +2 to pull punch and +1 on initiative stored flat. +1 to save vs Horror Factor at levels 2, 4, 8 and 12 is four at_level entries. +1 to strike/ensnare with a lasso at levels 2, 6 and 11 is conditional on the weapon and is a special ability, not a number. || SPECIAL SKILLS: Prospecting (40% +5%) is the catalog row at the class figure; Rope Works (30% +5%) is the catalog row at its own figure. || SKILL READINGS: Speaks Australian/English at 90% is Language: Australian English with no per-level step. Basic Math is Mathematics: Basic; General Athletics is Athletics (general); Pilot Automobile, Truck or Motorcycle (+5%) is one pick from Automobile, Truck and Motorcycles & Snowmobiles; Lore: One of choice (+10%) is one pick from the Lore rows open to Rifts. Horsemanship: Cowboy prints no bonus and is the catalog 66/3. Communication: except Laser is Laser Communications. Pilot: except Robot Elite, Power Armor and military vehicles is read as the twelve Robot Combat Elite rows, Robots & Power Armor with Robot Combat: Basic, and the five Military: pilot rows. Horsemanship: General and Exotic Animals are offered at the Pilot +10% because Rifts files horsemanship under Pilot, a reading. Secondary skills are two at each of levels 1, 3, 5, 8 and 11. Hand to Hand: never Assassin, so assassin is not priced. || MONEY: 2D6x$100 in dollars is starting_money; the 1D6x$100 in tradeable goods (the text layer prints lD6x$100) is in GM Notes. || EQUIPMENT not stored as rows: the clothes (cap or hat, shirt, singlet, jeans, boots, Sunday clothes), the S.D.C. sidearm with 1D4 clips or a crossbow and 24 bolts (a choice with its own ammunition), 1D4 old-style books of matches and the pet are in GM Notes. The M.D. energy rifle is stored as one generic weapon row. The rope row is the catalog rope priced per 40 feet; the book length is 60 feet."
---

## Lore

Anyone born in Australia outside the two Tech-Cities is an Outbacker. The
Runabout, also called a Drifter, Bush Cowboy or Cowpoke, is the Outbacker who
could not stay put: a rugged, unregimented wanderer who lives off the land
and drifts from one town or job to the next looking for opportunity,
adventure and a good time.

Runabouts have a name for being tough, honorable, blunt and unhurried. They
take things as they come, rarely complain, and can look like lazy drifters
right up to the moment someone crosses the line they will not see crossed;
then they are as fierce as anything in the Outback. They know a little of
everything, enough to get by, without being expert road warriors or
bushmen, and they love a rough, loud Outback town as much as the open
country.

## GM Notes

+1 to strike or ensnare with a lasso at levels 2, 6 and 11; the sheet does
not add it.

Anyone tied up by this character is -10% to escape. Identifying a fake with
Prospecting is at -10%.

Starting kit beyond what the sheet lists: the clothes on his back (cap or
hat, shirt, singlet, jeans, boots), a set of fancy Sunday clothes, either an
S.D.C. sidearm with 1D4 ammo clips or a crossbow and 24 bolts, one M.D.
energy rifle, and 1D4 old-style books of matches. Soap, a comb, a flashlight
or lantern, aspirin and the like are not included and must be bought with
starting funds. He often has a small animal as a pet: anything from a toad
or lizard to a dog or an exotic creature.

Transport: no horse or vehicle to start unless the G.M. says otherwise; he
is likely to pick up a riding animal, motorcycle or small vehicle in time.

Money: besides the cash, 1D6x$100 in tradeable goods.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'outbacker-runabout');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'outbacker-runabout';

